 - [ ] **REG-002**: When a lookup completes, the system SHALL include the active snapshot date in the result.
 - [ ] **REG-003**: When a snapshot has an invalid signature, an unsupported schema version, or duplicate serial numbers, the system SHALL reject the import and retain the active snapshot.
 - [ ] **REG-004**: When a valid replacement snapshot is activated, the system SHALL expose all of its records together without exposing a partially imported snapshot.
+- [ ] **REG-005**: When importing a snapshot, the system SHALL build a new SQLite database file in a staging directory, populate it with all records and metadata, validate it, and only then atomically replace the active database file.
+- [ ] **REG-006**: When a snapshot import fails at any step, the system SHALL leave the previous active database file unchanged and report an error identifying the failure stage.
+- [ ] **REG-007**: When a serial-number lookup executes, the system SHALL query the active SQLite database using a parameterized query and return the result within 250 ms for 90,000 records.
+- [ ] **REG-008**: When the active snapshot database is opened, the system SHALL read the snapshot date from the database metadata table and include it in every lookup result.
